.policy "ruff-fast002-fast-api-non-annotated-dependency" revision 2
.description "Declare FastAPI route dependencies and parameter markers inside Annotated type hints instead of as default values, so the function keeps ordinary defaults when called directly."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff FAST002 (FastAPI): a route function's parameter (not positional-only, not `*args`/`**kwargs`) with an
// annotation and a default that is a FastAPI marker: `Query`, `Path`, `Body`, `Cookie`, `Header`, `File`, `Form`
// (called or not), or the dependency `Depends`/`Security`. FastAPI reads the marker from `Annotated[T, marker]`
// as well, and the function then keeps a plain default. Reported at the parameter. Ruff's fix rewrites it to
// the Annotated form (unsafe); not offered here.
//   @app.get("/items/")
//   async def read(q: str = Query(""), db: Session = Depends(get_db)): …   ← FAST002 twice
//   async def read(q: Annotated[str, Query()] = "", db: Annotated[Session, Depends(get_db)]): …   not reported
#include "python/misc2-fastapi.rr"
//   fast_route(f, dc), fast_param(f, p, x, ann, dflt), fast_dependency(e, x)

.violation FAST002Marker(at: node, DEFAULT: node, NAME: symbol, TYPE: node) code "FAST002"
    "Move `{DEFAULT}` into `{NAME}: Annotated[{TYPE}, ...]`; if the call has a default argument, take it out of the call and keep it as the plain `= default`, dropping it when it is `...`."
    suppress ruff "FAST002"
.violation FAST002Dependency(at: node, DEFAULT: node, NAME: symbol, TYPE: node) code "FAST002"
    "Declare `{NAME}: Annotated[{TYPE}, {DEFAULT}]` instead of passing the dependency as the default; move the parameter before any with defaults, or make it keyword-only, if needed."
    suppress ruff "FAST002"
FAST002Marker(p, d, x, a) :- route_param(p, d, x, a, k), k != "Depends", k != "Security".
FAST002Dependency(p, d, x, a) :- route_param(p, d, x, a, k), (k = "Depends" ; k = "Security").
.decl route_param(p: node, d: node, x: symbol, a: node, k: symbol)
route_param(p, d, x, a, k) :- fast_route(f, _), fast_param(f, p, x, a, d), !unset(a), !unset(d),
    fast_dependency(d, k).
